  "prompt": "Product wants to know how often a session leads to a report. Use every app event in the data. A user's first app event starts a session, and an event more than 30 minutes after the same user's previous event starts a new one; an event exactly 30 minutes later stays in the same session. Measure each gap as the time between the two moments in event_ts, a UTC instant, never between clock times. For each account, give its users' number of sessions and the percentage of those sessions that include at least one export_report event, rounded to 1 decimal with ROUND (12.5 for 12.5%). Return three columns, in this order: account_id, sessions and export_session_pct. Return one row for each account with app events. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "account_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "sessions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "export_session_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
